# ==== ORPHAN-PRE-CLOSE · `meta if` ITEM blocks (AXIS A + AXIS E)
#
# The item-level `meta if` is the third face of the tail-orphan class: one
# producer, three arms. Each arm's flush needs its OWN ceiling — the NEXT
# clause's header — because with one ceiling for all three, the then-branch's
# flush swallows the elif branch's leading comment and documents the wrong
# branch.
#
# AXIS A cells: tail of the THEN branch · tail of the ELIF branch · tail of the
#   ELSE branch · the `meta if` STATEMENT body (a routed suite, not an item
#   block — the two live in different emitters).
#
# AXIS E cells (the per-branch CEILING, all NEGATIVE): the LEADING comment of
#   the elif branch's first item stays in the ELIF branch, and the same for the
#   else branch. Green on arrival; RED-verified by BREAK-AND-WATCH — widen
#   either ceiling to the whole `meta if`'s `span.end` and the leading comment
#   is pulled up into the branch ABOVE it.
#
# RED, observed on the pre-fix build: all four axis-A tails escaped to column 0.

meta if true:
    void then_one():
        print(1)
    # tail of the THEN branch
elif false:
    # leads the ELIF branch's first item
    void elif_one():
        print(2)
    # tail of the ELIF branch
else:
    # leads the ELSE branch's first item
    void else_one():
        print(3)
    # tail of the ELSE branch

void meta_if_statement_body(int x):
    meta if true:
        print(x)
        # tail of the meta-if STATEMENT body
    print(x)

void main():
    then_one()
    meta_if_statement_body(1)
